    //  the sensitivity. `fw_lay` says where they stand: 0 along the bottom, 1 fanned out of the four corners, 2 along the top, 3 down the left, 4 down the right. Each slot works out where its base is
    //  (`fwbx_*, fwby_*`: a point on the frame's inner edge, or the screen's edge without the frame) and which way it grows (`fwdx_*, fwdy_*`, a unit vector); the box is then centred
    //  half its length from the base, turned to point along it. Along an edge the `fw.n` slots in use are spread along it and mirrored about the middle (the bass, bar 0, at the centre, the highs at both ends,
